### About Dataset



* Derived from a real tyre retailer's transaction records. Brands, suppliers and product identifiers have been anonymised, and all monetary values scaled by a constant factor. Demand patterns, seasonality and relative price relationships are preserved; absolute monetary values do not represent real prices and should not be interpreted as such.



* Date - 2024–2026
* There are 3 tables in this dataset.



\------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------



### About Tables



1. **Current Stock**



&#x09;Point-in-time inventory snapshot covering 253 SKUs.
Gives stock on hand, unit cost and the last restock date for each product.
Joins to the sales file on Product ID.
Prices are in Indian Rupees.

&#x09;Size : 252 x 6

&#x09;Date Range : From 2019-12-24 to 2026-02-11



|**Columns**|**Meaning**|
|-|-|
|Product ID|SKU identifier (Primary key; joins to sales.csv)|
|Brand|Anonymised brand label (Joins to suppliers.csv)|
|Product Name|Tyre size and pattern code|
|Current Stock Quantity|Units on hand at snapshot date|
|Unit Cost|Purchase cost per tyre, scaled. (Compare with Unit Price for margin)|
|Last Restock Date|Most recent replenishment for this SKU|





2\.	**Sales**



&#x09;Daily transaction records for 259 tyre SKUs from April 2024 to March 2026.
Each row is one sale or return, with date, brand, product identifier, tyre size, units, unit price, revenue and the price tier the item sold at.

&#x09;Returns appear as negative units and negative revenue.

&#x09;Size : 17000 x 9

&#x09;Date Range : From 2024-04-08 to 2026-03-31



|**Columns**|**Meaning**|
|-|-|
|Date|Transaction date. Daily granularity, Apr 2024 – Mar 2026|
|Brand|Anonymised brand label. Four values, one per supplier|
|Product ID|SKU identifier (P0001 format). Joins to current\_stock.csv|
|Product Name|Tyre size and pattern code (e.g. 215/70 R 16 TR28 OWL)|
|Units Sold|Quantity (Positive for sales, negative for returns)|
|Unit Price|Price per tyre, scaled. (Always positive, including on returns)|
|Revenue|Units × unit price. (Negative on returns)|
|Transaction Type|Sale or Return|
|Price Tier|Price tier the item sold at: A (93%), X, P, U|





3\.	**Supplier**



&#x09;Lead time profile for the four suppliers, one per brand.

&#x09;Includes average, minimum, maximum and standard deviation of lead time in days, for use in reorder point and safety stock calculations.

&#x09;Joins to both other files on Brand.

&#x09;Size : 5 x 7



|**Columns**|**Meaning**|
|-|-|
|Brand|Anonymised brand label. Primary key; joins to the other two files|
|Supplier ID|Supplier identifier (SUP0001 format)|
|Supplier Name|Anonymised supplier name|
|Avg Lead Time|Mean days from order to delivery|
|Lead Time Std Dev (days)|Estimated variability|
|Min Lead Time (days)|Fastest observed delivery|
|Max Lead Time (days)|Slowest observed delivery|

